hers animated  which also kind of reminds me i don't  know why warner brothers doesn't just  focus on their animated movies maybe  because people look at animated movies  and see them as kind of silly  and a little bit childish i don't really  know why they love going to movie  theaters and watching movies about how a  guy is exposed to gamma radiation and  turns into a giant green rage monster  not really sure how you split the  difference i mean at the end of the day  if you can call the avengers movie  a comic book movie that's awesome i  don't know why you can't do the same  thing for animated films  after all the lion king's the greatest  animated film of all time and nobody  calls that silly or childish but i  really wish that warner brothers would  just  focus on their comic book animated line  and just leave the live action movies in  the dust because they have just been  bad consistently but the animated movies  have been great consistently i wish they  would just focus on that but regardless  dc's gods among us is going to be an  awesome film and i cannot  wait for this movie to come out having  said that moving into our last bit of  news here focusing on the young avengers  actor jack veal who played kid loki in  the loki tv show  was recently asked about what his  thoughts were in appearing in the young  avengers and what he basically revealed  is he has not heard anything about it  yet now  that does not mean it's not going to  happen and it does not mean he's not  going to be in it  we know young avengers is going to  happen it's only a matter of time but we  also know that paul bettany  and elizabeth olsen were basically hit  up at the 11th hour to see if they  wanted to do a one division tv show like  literally it was like a napkin idea and  they just launched it right so  it's one of these things where if the  the marvel cinematic universe and disney  are keeping this really close to the  vest  these guys won't even notice a project  until right before it launches and so  even if they do know they've probably  been sworn to secrecy under pain of  death  and they can't tell us but regardless of  the situation  i do want to see jack veal and the young  avengers as kid loki  i think he'd be a perfect addition to  the marvel cinematic universe as a  greater whole  and in all honesty i think that's one of  the things you're going to see in a lot  of the shows going forward right you're  going to see the introduction of  characters here and there  that marvel's basically going to kind of  throw to us and say hey like what do you  guys think about this character what do  you think about that character  not so much in terms of hitting it on  the nose and asking us directly  but by just kind of revealing them to us  over the course of the shows and seeing  how we respond  in terms of our our whole position on  social media for example  there was a whole argument that took  place between whether or not the loki  alligator that we saw was either an  alligator or a crocodile  there was this huge debate that was  happening on twitter it was just it was  explosive everybody was just kind of  going back and forth  over whether it was an alligator or  crocodile but regardless that kind of  stuff right there is really what helps  to determine  what characters are the most popular and  which ones aren't and so because of that  i feel like  having jack veal as kid loki and young  avengers would be great it'd be a great  addition to the young avengers landscape  but let me know what you guys think down  in the comments section but regardless  we're gonna bring this to an end thank  you guys for watching  and i will catch you all later peace
 

